Prologe: To Skills, Plugins, and Governance in the Enterprise

We went through a rapid development cycle the last few years that took us from chating with a model to building skills and plugins that let the model act in the world. This series of posts is about what I learned along the way, and how to apply it in your organization. My plan is to write six posts, each one a chapter in the story of how we got from prompts to skills to plugins to governance. I dug deep into my educational history and outlined the whole series before writing this first post. I very much felt reminded of the old day's writing 10 page papers about crutial topics like Lincolns Getisburg Address. I hope tht this series will find more real life application than those papers did, and that it will be useful to you in your work. I also hope it will be a fun read, and that you will enjoy the journey as much as I enjoyed writing it. 

I think that alot has been said already about the best developer setup and plugins and practices. My focuse is on the enablement of the knowledge workers in the enterprise and how to equip them at enterprise scale with the right tools.

I am using Generative AI to write this series of posts. I am using Claude for the Outline and GitHub Copilot is my assistant to help me with the writing, but I am indentional about my writing. My goals is to write in my own style and voice and in a way that I enjoy reading it myself and I am not a fan of reading just AI Generated content myself so this is a lot of hands on the keybord for me with feedback from my Assistant to keep me from rambeling.